---
import Public from "../layouts/Public.astro";
---

<Public title="Privacy" description="How Token Flame Graph handles data and security.">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px; padding: 4rem 1rem;">
    <h1 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      Last updated: April 9, 2026
    </p>
    <p>
      Token Flame Graph collects operational telemetry you intentionally send through the SDK (for example session IDs,
      timing, token counts, and metadata fields). We use this data only to provide observability, cost analysis, and
      reliability features for your workspace.
    </p>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Data We Store</h2>
    <ul style="padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.8;">
      <li>Workspace and account identifiers</li>
      <li>Session and event traces submitted by SDK clients</li>
      <li>Hashed API keys (never raw keys after creation)</li>
      <li>Alert configurations and alert fire metadata</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Security</h2>
    <p>
      We apply workspace isolation controls, authenticated API access, and key hashing for credential storage. Access to
      production systems is restricted to authorized operators.
    </p>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:privacy@eddieai.online">privacy@eddieai.online</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Public>
